# Vendored subset of llama.cpp common/ — HEADERS ONLY
# Upstream: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
# Pinned commit: 3e12fbdea5c1ac4225c7dcf79506d30950283fc3
# Bottled by Homebrew as llama.cpp b9200
#
# Implementations live in libllama-common (Homebrew dylib). We vendor only
# the headers needed to consume the chat/template/PEG API from CLlamaBridge.
# Must come from the exact commit recorded above so that the C++ ABI matches
# the Homebrew-installed libllama-common.
#
# Re-vendor procedure (when Homebrew bumps llama.cpp, e.g. to b9201):
#
#   # 1. Identify the new commit SHA matching the new Homebrew bottle:
#   gh api repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/refs/tags/b9201 --jq '.object.sha'
#
#   # 2. Clone at that SHA:
#   rm -rf /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp.git /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned
#   cd /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned
#   git fetch --depth 1 origin <NEW_SHA> && git checkout <NEW_SHA>
#
#   # 3. Refresh the headers (DEST is the directory containing this file):
#   DEST=Sources/CLlamaBridge/third_party/llama_cpp_common
#   cp /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned/common/{chat,common,log,peg-parser,regex-partial}.h "$DEST/"
#   cp /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned/common/{chat-peg-parser,chat-auto-parser,chat-auto-parser-helpers}.h "$DEST/"
#   cp /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned/common/{json-schema-to-grammar,unicode}.h "$DEST/"
#   cp /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned/common/jinja/*.h "$DEST/jinja/"
#   cp /tmp/llama-cpp-pinned/vendor/nlohmann/{json,json_fwd}.hpp "$DEST/nlohmann/"
#
#   # 4. Update this file (the SHA and bottle number above).
#   # 5. Update local-llm/README.md (same).
#   # 6. swift build && swift test  — catches ABI drift early.
